WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.280
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going to&nbsp;
explain an American comedy-heist film called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:19.280
“The Perfect Score”. Watch out and take care!
Kyle is a normal high school senior aiming to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:25.920
into Cornell University’s architecture program.&nbsp;
He knows exactly what he wants in life but the SAT&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.680
is standing in between him and his dreams. In&nbsp;
the opening scene, he is in the examination hall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.960
looking through the answer sheet that is telling&nbsp;
him he is just an average guy. After the examiner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:44.960
asks them to stop writing, Kyle looks around and&nbsp;
locks eyes with Anna. She has a 4.0 GPA and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.320
the second-highest-ranking student of the school.&nbsp;
Which makes it surprising that her answer sheet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.600
is completely blank. In the background, it is&nbsp;
narrated that students might be good at different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.600
things; some are better at singing and others&nbsp;
at sports. But according to the SAT, everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:07.600
has to pass a “standardized” examination that will&nbsp;
determine their future. The narrator thinks it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:16.400
unfair, so he calls the SATs, a Suck Ass Test. 
The results are published and Kyle scores 1020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:22.560
as opposed to the minimum 1430 that he needs to&nbsp;
get into his preferred college. He complains to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.240
the principal about the absurd method that the&nbsp;
SAT uses to test the students. According to Kyle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.280
math equations and complicated social scenarios&nbsp;
are not the way to determine if a student should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.560
get to go to their dream college. The principal&nbsp;
receives hundreds of students after every test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.040
complaining about how unfair it is. But&nbsp;
all of them have one thing in common;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.160
their score is less than what they&nbsp;
need. For him, Kyle is just one of many,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:54.640
so he dismisses the conversation after giving him&nbsp;
lousy advice that he delivers to every student.
&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:01.040
Then, we are introduced to Matty, Kyle’s dumb&nbsp;
best friend, and his right-hand man. He has an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:08.720
average GPA of 2.3 and is not so good at studying.&nbsp;
Matty’s girlfriend Sandy is a freshman in Maryland&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:14.000
college so his only goal in life is to join&nbsp;
Maryland and hook up with her one more time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.720
Kyle tells him that he lied to his parents&nbsp;
about scoring 1430. The poor fellows even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:24.320
bought him a cake to congratulate him. His elder&nbsp;
brother Larry is a bigger idiot than Matty.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.480
He lives on top of his parents’ garage that&nbsp;
he claims is a different house because it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.840
has a separate phone line. Larry accidentally&nbsp;
blows the 0 from the candles and jokes about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:41.040
how he got a 143 SAT score back in his day. 
Later, the friends go to the Educational Testing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:47.760
Service center, commonly known as ETS to complain&nbsp;
about the unfair system. However, the receptionist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.120
stops them because many students like them come&nbsp;
to complain about their SAT scores every day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:59.440
As they are asked to go away, a girl proudly walks&nbsp;
inside the building. She is the talk of the town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:05.600
and the dream of every high school guy, Francesca.&nbsp;
She walks into the building like she owns it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:11.920
which is untrue because her father is the one who&nbsp;
owns it. That evening, Kyle and Matty drink while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.440
thinking of a way to ace the next test. Matty&nbsp;
calls his girlfriend Sandy but a man picks up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:23.280
her phone. The call ends in only a second but&nbsp;
Matty registers that she is cheating on him.
&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.240
He blames the SATs and suggests they&nbsp;
steal the answers for the next test.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:34.400
Kyle laughs it off at first but starts to take the&nbsp;
idea into consideration. The next time they meet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:40.240
he asks Matty if they were to “borrow” the answer&nbsp;
sheets from ETS, how would they go about it. Matty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.080
suggests they ask Francesca for help since she&nbsp;
can enter the ETS headquarters anytime she wants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.600
Moreover, she is an adrenaline junkie and will&nbsp;
do anything to have fun. A heist is right up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.160
her alley so the guys are positive she will&nbsp;
join them. When she is briefed about the plan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:02.400
she immediately agrees. Then, we are introduced&nbsp;
to a star basketball player Desmond. He plans to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.440
join St. John’s university and play for their&nbsp;
team. Even the dean is happy to have him. 
&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.440
However, he has to take the SATs and score&nbsp;
at least 900 to get into college. Desmond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.560
is excellent at math but that would still not be&nbsp;
enough for him to make it. Kyle and Matty are in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:24.400
the school’s bathroom when Kyle reveals that he&nbsp;
told the school topper, Anna, about their plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.920
He has a crush on her but refuses to admit it.&nbsp;
Matty freaks out because she is one of the nerds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:35.200
who will probably tell the police but Kyle assures&nbsp;
him they are fine because she refused to be a part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:39.840
of their plan anyway. The two had thought they&nbsp;
were alone in the bathroom and are surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:46.000
when the school junkie Roy appears in one of the&nbsp;
stalls. Kyle and Matty hope that he is too high to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.680
understand what they said but the guy is used to&nbsp;
being highly alert even when high. At last, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:56.960
have to reluctantly include him in the plan. 
At night, Anna returns home to see that her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.840
parents have called a professor from Brown to&nbsp;
help her get into the university. She is tired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:06.320
of them pushing her to do better because doesn’t&nbsp;
even want to go to an Ivy League university in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:12.000
the first place. Since she zoned out in the last&nbsp;
SAT, they have been pressuring her more than ever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:18.560
The next morning, Francesca, Kyle, Matty, and Roy&nbsp;
go to the ETS headquarter and devise a plan for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:23.600
a simple heist. Francesca provides them with&nbsp;
the uniforms from the mailroom and makes them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:29.280
enter the ETS floor without any problem. They&nbsp;
had asked Roy to stay outside but he somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:34.480
enters the building on his own and includes&nbsp;
himself in the plan. Then, the group separates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:40.080
and goes around the office trying to figure out&nbsp;
which cabin has the SAT answer sheet. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:46.240
in the school library, Desmond meets Anna and asks&nbsp;
her to help him to prepare for the SAT. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:51.200
Anna herself is stressed about the test and is&nbsp;
scared she will mess up again. She thinks of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:56.320
joining Kyle on his heist and also tells Desmond&nbsp;
about the plan, hoping it would help him.
&nbsp;

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:01.120
Back in the headquarters, a woman finds Roy&nbsp;
snooping through her office. She is about to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:07.200
report him but he uses his poor flirting skills to&nbsp;
make her stop. Even though his pick-up lines are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.840
lame, she seems to enjoy them. In the other room,&nbsp;
an office worker calls Kyle and hands him the SAT&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:19.360
question sheet. Kyle is left stunned but it&nbsp;
turns out that the man mistook him for a worker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:25.840
in the copy room. He asks Kyle to print two copies&nbsp;
of the paper and hand them back. Kyle happily goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:31.760
to the copy room but accidentally shreds the paper&nbsp;
instead of copying it. They are back to square one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:37.360
because of his stupidity. Following that, Anna&nbsp;
meets Kyle and asks to be included in the plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.400
along with Desmond. Kyle had lost hope but&nbsp;
now that Anna wants to be a part of the plan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.560
he thinks of another way to acquire the&nbsp;
paper. He collects the blueprint of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:51.520
building from Francesca and asks her to&nbsp;
get all the security codes. Anna spies on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:56.880
headquarter’s security guard and finds out the&nbsp;
routine of the rounds he takes every night.
&nbsp;

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:02.240
Then, they decide to meet at Kyle’s brother’s&nbsp;
place to go over the plan one last time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:08.080
While Francesca is coding something, Roy helps&nbsp;
her, proving that he is a technical genius. Kyle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:18.000
keeps it in mind because they might need his&nbsp;
help in case of an emergency. Then, he explains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:23.520
the plan in brief. Although it is a little shaky&nbsp;
and success isn’t guaranteed, the group agrees to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:29.440
help him. The next day, Roy, Desmond, and Anna&nbsp;
stay outside the ETS headquarters to keep an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:34.720
eye on the building’s guard. Meanwhile, Kyle&nbsp;
and Matty enter the building and wait until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:40.720
the top floor is cleared. When all the employees&nbsp;
go home, Francesca distracts the security guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:45.280
giving the two an opportunity to run to&nbsp;
the roof. From there, they use a rope to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:50.080
enter the topmost floor and get to the room&nbsp;
where the papers were supposed to be kept.
&nbsp;

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:55.200
However, it turns out that the floor has been&nbsp;
renovated since the blueprint was made, and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.200 --> 00:08:00.320
do not know where the papers are. They refuse to&nbsp;
return empty-handed and start brainstorming other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:06.000
ideas. Kyle remembers that the man who ordered him&nbsp;
to print the papers also has a copy on his desk.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:11.040
They go to his office and start looking around&nbsp;
with their torchlights. Just then, the security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:16.640
guard steps outside to smoke. The flashes of their&nbsp;
lights are clearly visible from the guard’s view&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:21.920
so Anna quickly calls the group to alert them.&nbsp;
They turn the lights off seconds before the guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.640
sees them. After that, they finally find the room&nbsp;
they are looking for but the answer sheets are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:32.160
nowhere to be found. As the last resort, they try&nbsp;
to open the computer but it requires a password.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:37.200
They call the technical genius, Roy, for help.&nbsp;
But they will have to distract the guard before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.160
letting him in. This time, Matty comes up&nbsp;
with a plan and calls his friend to deliver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:46.800
flowers and alcohol to the guard’s name. 
When the guard is busy receiving the gifts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:53.040
Roy runs inside. Along with him, Anna and Desmond&nbsp;
also come, thinking that they might be of help.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:58.080
Then, Roy predicts the password using a picture&nbsp;
on the table. The group finally gets their hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:03.200
on the question paper but to print it out, they&nbsp;
will need three more passwords. They lose all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:08.960
hope and are about to return but Kyle refuses to&nbsp;
give up. He says that they can solve the answers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:13.760
in the time before the guard comes for a routine&nbsp;
round. Everyone else laughs at him because if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:17.920
could answer the questions, they wouldn’t have&nbsp;
to be there in the first place. He reads the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.640
first question out loud and Anna answers it&nbsp;
instantly. She couldn’t answer the questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:28.160
in a classroom because of stress but when she&nbsp;
is with them, she can easily solve the paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:33.920
Desmond is also excellent at math, so he and Roy&nbsp;
solve the math portion of the test while Anna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:39.520
and Kyle solve the verbal. Lastly, Francesca&nbsp;
and Matty are told to watch the lobby. 
&nbsp;

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:43.600
While waiting, they get into a conversation&nbsp;
about Matty’s girlfriend Sandy who doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:49.600
call him anymore. Francesca tells him that it is&nbsp;
over and asks him to get over her but Matty gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:55.440
irritated by the comment. Suddenly, she kisses&nbsp;
him and claims that he would be a good boyfriend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:01.360
to whoever he loves. A while later, they get done&nbsp;
with the questions and finally get ready to leave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:05.920
Roy tries to climb up first but the others&nbsp;
pull him down, noticing that he has stolen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:10.640
supplies from the office. Desmond makes him&nbsp;
put them back in their places while the others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:16.160
continue climbing up. Anna and Kyle easily make&nbsp;
it to the top but the security guard comes for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:22.640
the rounds before the others can escape. Desmond,&nbsp;
Matty, and Roy are in the safe zone but Francesca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:27.280
is about to be caught. At that moment,&nbsp;
Matty decides to come in front of the guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:31.840
to save her. While the others climb to the&nbsp;
rooftop, he surrenders and is arrested.
&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:41.840
The next morning, Francesca steals money from her&nbsp;
father and bails Matty out. They reunite and kiss.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:46.160
Matty doesn’t want to take the SATs anymore&nbsp;
because he thinks he is better off not going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:51.520
to college. He wants to take a year off to find&nbsp;
out what he wants to be in life. Anna is also a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:56.240
different person from who she was yesterday. She&nbsp;
stands up to her mother for the first time and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:01.920
declares that she isn’t going to Brown. Following&nbsp;
that, the group gathers and Kyle hands them the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:07.600
answers. However, Anna refuses to take them&nbsp;
because she wants to go to Europe for college.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:13.360
Desmond and Roy also do not want it because Roy&nbsp;
wants to start creating online games and Desmond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:19.040
has gained confidence after solving the questions&nbsp;
during the heist. Francesca, who already had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:26.640
perfect SAT score has no use for the answers and&nbsp;
Matty is also not taking the test. At last, Kyle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:32.000
too, refuses to use them. Because they are&nbsp;
of no use now, Roy hands them to his junkie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:37.840
friends who ace their test because of it.
A few months later, Desmond takes the retest and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:43.680
gets into his desired university. Matty starts&nbsp;
to audition for acting roles while Francesca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.960
sells her first novel. Kyle also does fine on&nbsp;
his re-test. Although he doesn’t get into his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:54.480
preferred college, he still dreams of being an&nbsp;
architect. Anna, on the other hand, moves to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.480 --> 00:12:00.320
Europe for further studies. She starts dating Kyle&nbsp;
and frequently returns to New York to meet him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:06.400
Lastly, Roy sells a hit online game making&nbsp;
millions of dollars. In the ending scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.040
we see him living his best life. 
